codex
Defect: lines 80-84, instrument reads a different copy than the one changed.  
Exact input: `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_FULL_REVIEW.html` contains required matched blocks but existing visible/verdict text says `OR 9.999`; `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_REVIEW.html` likewise says `OR 9.999`.  
Consequence: the “nothing numeric may move” guard still passes because it checks only hardcoded module constants, then rewrites target HTML numbers and prints “unchanged”.

Defect: line 327, selector keyed to one exact script spelling.  
Exact input: `<script>\nwindow.__RM_ALLOW_PHASE2_POOLING = true;\nwindow.__verdict = {};\nwindow.__quarantinedTrials = {};</script>`  
Consequence: semantically equivalent HTML/JS is not matched, so the repair aborts with `verdict script block not found`.

Defect: lines 343-349 and 486-492, case-sensitive/off-by-one HTML div scanner with no “found closing tag” assertion.  
Exact input: `<div id="rapidmeta-integrity-badge">old</DIV><p>must remain</p>`  
Consequence: valid HTML with uppercase close is treated as unterminated, so replacement consumes through EOF and silently drops following content before printing success.

Defect: line 512, selector keyed to exact spacing around assignment.  
Exact input: `<script>window.__verdict={"verdict":"OLD"};</script>`  
Consequence: valid existing stub verdict is missed and the script aborts with `stub verdict not found`.

No proven `or {}` / `or 0` zero-vs-absent defect found.  
No proven negation-dropped extraction defect found.  
No proven CRLF/LF text-comparison defect found.  
COULD NOT DETERMINE actual corpus selector coverage: missing `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_FULL_REVIEW.html` and `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_REVIEW.html` contents.
